<section class="intro">
  <h1>Vicenzo Ribas Másera</h1>
  <p>I build iOS apps — a game shipped to the App Store with a five-person team, <em class="accent">on-device machine learning that never makes a network call</em>, a real-time tool that keeps a room of people in sync over WebSockets. Most of this happened at the Apple Developer Academy, where I shipped three native products from zero to release across iPhone and Mac.</p>
  <p>I gravitate toward architecture that holds up under other people’s hands: reducers and protocol boundaries over shortcuts only the original author understands. That instinct sharpens the larger the team around the code gets — I’ve worked inside a roughly 50-person squad organization, where legibility mattered more than cleverness.</p>
</section>
